{"id":"word:hebrew:H7138","type":"word","title":"קָרוֹב","subtitle":"H7138 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"near (in place, kindred or time)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קָרוֹב (H7138) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 78 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קָרוֹב (qârôwb) means near (in place, kindred or time) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 12 41."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קָרוֹב","transliteration":"qârôwb","pronunciation":"kaw-robe'","strong":"H7138","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7138","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["קָרוֹב֙","קָר֥וֹב","קָר֣וֹב","קָר֤וֹב","קָר֖וֹב"],"morphs":[["HAamsa",32],["HTd/Aampa",7],["HAampa",7],["HAafsa",6],["HR/Aamsa",5],["HTd/Aamsa",4],["HAamsc/Sp3ms",3],["HC/Aamsa",3],["HTd/Aafsa",2],["HC/Td/Aamsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"near (in place, kindred or time)","usage":"allied, approach, at hand, any of kin, kinsfold(-sman), (that is) near (of kin), neighbour, (that is) next, (them that come) nigh (at hand), more ready, short(-ly).","full":"H7138. qarob קָרוֺב קָרֹב, 78 adjective near ; — absolute קָרֹב Exod 12:4 +, וֺב - 2 Samuel 19:48 +; plural קְרֹבִים 1Kin 8:59 , קְרוֺבִים Isa 33:13 +; feminine plural קְרֹבוֺת Ezek 22:5 , etc.; &#8212; near (often opposed to רָחוֺק ) : 1 of city Gen 19:20 (+ שָׁ֫מָּה לָנוּס ), Jer 48:24 , ׳הַקּ Deut 21:3 the nearest (+ אֶל ), compare (of elders) 21:6 ; of land 1Kin 8:46 2Chr 6:36 ; road Exod 13:17 ; = contiguous, כֶּרֶם 1Kin 21:2 (+ בֵּיתִי אֵצֶל ). 2 of person: a. + אֶל person Gen 45:10 ; Deut 13:8 ; 22:2 ; Josh 9:16 ; 1 Chronicles 12:41 (van d. H. v40); ׳הַקּ אֶל Exod 12:4 the nearest to ; with suffix קְרֹבוֺ 32:27 , i.e. his neighbour . b. absolute (opposed to or + רחוק , oft,= near and far , i.e. all without distinction), Ezek 6:12 ; Isa 57:19 ; Prov 27:10 ; plural Isa 33:13 ; Jer 25:26 ; Dan 9:7 ; Est 9:20 ; Exod 22:5 ; ׳ק of distress, personified, Psa 22:12 .; &#8212; Ezek 23:5 , 12 Co Berthol read קְרוּאִים famous ; Toy רַבִּים (compare Jer 39:13 ); Hpt in Toy Krae conjectures קְרוֺדִים (Assyrian ‡urâ du , warrior ). c. of near relationship , + אֶל person2 Sam Jeremiah 19:43; Lev 21:2-3 , 25:25 (all H), Num 27:11 (P); ל pers Neh 13:4 ; Ruth 2:20 ; + מִן compare 3:12 ; of intimacy, קְרֹנוֺ Psa 15:3 (|| רֵעֵהוּ ), קְרוֺבַי Job 19:14 (|| מְיֻדָּעַי ) Psa 38:12 (|| וְרֵעַי אֹהֲנַי ); near , in office, Est 1:14 . d. near to י קְרֹבוֺ ׳עַם Psa 148:14 (Ri Bae קְרכָו the people of those near him ). e. near to ׳י in ceremon function, with אֶל Ezek 43:19 , with ל 42:13 , suffix Lev 10:3 . f. of God ( ׳י ), + אֶל person Deut 4:7 ; 30:14 ; ל pers Psa 34:19 ; 145:18 ; abs Jer 12:2 ; Isa 50:8 ; 55:6 Psa 119:151 ; מִקָּרֹב אֱלֹהֵי Jer 23:23 a God from near by (opposed to ׳א מֵרָחוֺק ); ׳ק of י ׳צֶרֶק Isa 51:5 , י ׳יֶשַׁע Psa 85:10 (+ ל of person); — שִׁמְךָ ׳ק 75:2 , read בְּשׁ ׳קֹרְאֵי Dy Che Gr Dr, compare Bae ᵐ5 SyeVer Du. g. of word , + אֶל person Deut 30:14 ; prayer, + ׳אֶליֿ 1Kin 8:59 . 3 of time : ׳ק אֵידָם יוֺם Deut 32:35 ; especially of י ׳יוֺם Zeph 1:7 , 14 (twice in verse); Ezek 30:3 (perhaps del as ᵐ5 Co Krae), 30:3 ; Isa 13:6 ; Obadiah 15; Joel 1:15 ; 2:1 ; Joel 4:14, compare Ezek 7:7 ; + infinitive ׳ק לָבוֺא אֵירמֿוֺאָב Jer 48:16 , compare Isa 13:22 ; 56:1 ; ק ׳מְחִתָּה Prov 10:14 imminent ruin ; מִקָּרוֺכ Deut 32:17 recently , so Ezek 11:3 ᵑ6 ᵐ5 Co Siegf Berthol (for Mt בְּקָרוֺב ) 7:8 soon ; Job 20:5 of the briefest ; — ק ׳אוֺר חשֶׁח מִמְּנֵי 17:12 is dubious; Thes (my) light is near to (prope abest a, as Arabic , but not proven in Hebrew) darkness ; Di light (they say) is near (breaking away) from darkness , will soon leave it behind; But מֶּןיֶֿחְשַׁךְ קְרוֺבָם אוֺר the light of their intimate friend shall not (?)grow dark .","rootNote":"or קָרֹב ; from 7126 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 12 41","keyReferences":["1Chr 12 41","